Chapter: Cities
  cites Uoaix chapter MapCache
  cites Uoaix chapter BritainWindow
  cites Uoaix chapter BritainCatalog

  CtCity = record { name : Text, x1 : Integer, y1 : Integer, x2 : Integer, y2 : Integer }
 A city's rectangle spans its UOX3 keeper and townsfolk spawn regions (data/dfndata/spawn/felucca/spawn_felucca_town_<city>.dfn);
 its walk window widens that to whole 8-tile blocks with at least a tile beside every edge. City 0 is Britain, whose window
 is BritainWindow's and whose map is the town map. A city's index is its place in this table; a new city is appended.
  ct-table : Integer -> List CtCity
  ct-table (unused) = [CtCity { name = "Britain", x1 = bwn-x1, y1 = bwn-y1, x2 = bwn-x2, y2 = bwn-y2 },
    CtCity { name = "Trinsic", x1 = 1811, y1 = 2643, x2 = 2075, y2 = 2912 },
    CtCity { name = "Moonglow", x1 = 4374, y1 = 1041, x2 = 4529, y2 = 1176 },
    CtCity { name = "Yew", x1 = 497, y1 = 769, x2 = 696, y2 = 1250 },
    CtCity { name = "Wind", x1 = 5146, y1 = 19, x2 = 5351, y2 = 191 },
    CtCity { name = "Skara Brae", x1 = 545, y1 = 2120, x2 = 671, y2 = 2285 },
    CtCity { name = "Ocllo", x1 = 3600, y1 = 2470, x2 = 3694, y2 = 2665 },
    CtCity { name = "Magincia", x1 = 3657, y1 = 2122, x2 = 3766, y2 = 2269 },
    CtCity { name = "Nujel'm", x1 = 3544, y1 = 1166, x2 = 3773, y2 = 1400 },
    CtCity { name = "Jhelom", x1 = 1305, y1 = 3672, x2 = 1534, y2 = 4061 },
    CtCity { name = "Serpent's Hold", x1 = 2860, y1 = 3338, x2 = 3067, y2 = 3527 },
    CtCity { name = "Buccaneer's Den", x1 = 2622, y1 = 2070, x2 = 2764, y2 = 2266 },
    CtCity { name = "Vesper", x1 = 2738, y1 = 618, x2 = 3040, y2 = 1003 },
    CtCity { name = "Minoc", x1 = 2417, y1 = 337, x2 = 2573, y2 = 679 },
    CtCity { name = "Cove", x1 = 2208, y1 = 1112, x2 = 2286, y2 = 1234 }]
  ct-x : CtCity -> Integer
  ct-x (c) = (c.x1 - 1) / 8 * 8
  ct-y : CtCity -> Integer
  ct-y (c) = (c.y1 - 1) / 8 * 8
  ct-width : CtCity -> Integer
  ct-width (c) = ((c.x2 + 1) / 8 + 1) * 8 - ct-x c
  ct-height : CtCity -> Integer
  ct-height (c) = ((c.y2 + 1) / 8 + 1) * 8 - ct-y c
 The city whose rectangle holds x, y, or -1.
  ct-city-at : List CtCity, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  ct-city-at (cities) (x) (y) (i) = if i >= list-length cities then -1
    else let c = list-at cities i
    in if x >= c.x1 & x <= c.x2 & y >= c.y1 & y <= c.y2 then i else ct-city-at cities x y (i + 1)
  ct-map-of : List WalkMap, Integer -> Maybe WalkMap
  ct-map-of (maps) (i) = if i < 0 | i >= list-length maps then None else Just (list-at maps i)
 The map of the city holding x, y, or None.
  ct-map-at : List CtCity, List WalkMap, Integer, Integer -> Maybe WalkMap
  ct-map-at (cities) (maps) (x) (y) = ct-map-of maps (ct-city-at cities x y 0)
 Every city's map in table order: city 0 is the Britain map already loaded; each other window is sized by its own busiest
 cell (wmc-window-colliders) and filled from the map cache.
  ct-load : MapCacheState, MapInstallData, List CtCity, WalkMap, Integer, List WalkMap -> [Device.Block] Result (List WalkMap) Text
  ct-load (cache) (installed) (cities) (britain) (i) (maps) = if i >= list-length cities then act Ok maps end
    else if i == 0 then ct-load cache installed cities britain 1 (maps & [britain])
    else let c = list-at cities i
    in act
      counted <- wmc-window-colliders cache (ct-x c) (ct-y c) (ct-width c) (ct-height c) installed
      when counted
        is Err (e) -> Err (c.name & " window: " & e)
        is Ok (colliders) -> when walk-map-sized (ct-x c) (ct-y c) (ct-width c) (ct-height c) (max 1 colliders)
          is Err (e) -> act Err (c.name & " window: " & e) end
          is Ok (map) -> act
            filled <- wmc-fill cache map 0
            when filled
              is Err (e) -> Err (c.name & " window: " & e)
              is Ok (_) -> ct-load cache installed cities britain (i + 1) (maps & [map])
          end
    end
  ct-said : List CtCity, List WalkMap, Integer, Text -> Text
  ct-said (cities) (maps) (i) (acc) = if i >= list-length maps | i >= list-length cities then acc
    else let m = list-at maps i
    in ct-said cities maps (i + 1) (acc & " " & (list-at cities i).name & " " & show m.width & "x" & show m.height & " stride=" & show m.stride)

 Every other city's shops follow Britain's in the vendor table: city shop k is vendor bb-shop-count + k and sells the
 goods of the Britain shop ct-shop-roles names (its index in bb-shops). Each row is a Britain BbShop: the role's title,
 the premises, and the keeper's UOX3 spawn region (spawn_felucca_town_<city>.dfn), in which the keeper stands. A city
 appends its rows to ct-city-shops and its roles to ct-shop-roles in the same order.
